    text+=f'## Inputs and expected results\n\nUse [the contract fixture](../../fixtures/storage/{pid}.json) and the actual C tests `{", ".join(tests)}`. The image has 67 pages of 4096 bytes; the tree owns 32 logical data pages. The reference transaction changes the complete map from {{1:10,2:20}} to {{1:11,3:30}}. Compare whole maps. No fixture asserts physical power-cut durability.\n\n'
    text+=f'## Steps\n\n1. Predict the state transitions on paper, naming capacities, ownership and the earliest invalid state.\n2. Implement this milestone in your external learner workspace; reveal only the next relevant stage of the hint table when blocked.\n3. Run the named positive and negative C cases and preserve exact commands, source identity, seed/cut and return codes.\n4. Explain one rejected result using the invariant, then repair and rerun the same trigger.\n5. Revisit an unfamiliar variation without hints and record separate evidence for {tid}.a, .b and .c.\n\n'
    text+=f'## Failure cases\n\n{fail}\n\nAn unavailable compiler, sanitizer runtime, syscall or device produces unavailable evidence; it never counts as a clean run. A wrong implementation must fail a semantic assertion after successful setup.\n\n'
    text+=f'## Acceptance and evidence\n\nDeliver the invariant/cost argument for .a, actual C/build/test transcript for .b, and minimized failure plus repaired and delayed transfer results for .c. Include the exact source-reading locator and fault assumptions. A CTest family pass supports its executed cases, not automatic completion of every objective. Use `tools/verify_storage_fixtures.py` for contract-index consistency; it neither compiles your C nor awards runtime mastery.\n\n'
    text+=f'## Hints and recovery\n\n{teaching}\n\nThe staged laboratory hints separate invariant, observation and repair direction. Keep the original failing image or key sequence and compare it with a clean control.\n\n## Transfer challenge\n\n{transfer}\n'
