text='```json\n'+json.dumps(meta,ensure_ascii=False,indent=2)+'\n```\n\n# T47: Persistent storage engine and crash consistency\n\n## Purpose and outcomes\n\nBuild a bounded B+tree store whose success and failure semantics survive a declared crash model. Derive byte encoding, ordered index invariants, memory/page bounds and persistence ordering before optimizing. This is one engine grown through small projects, not twelve independent database implementations. All values are length-delimited bytes; the C core has no SQL or external storage-engine dependency.\n\n## Entry check and remediation\n\nImplement a bounds-checked byte decoder, an ordered search invariant and a partial-I/O loop from memory. Explain object lifetime, unsigned conversion, stale cache data and why write return is not a persistence barrier. If these fail, return to T03/T15/T21 and reproduce the exact missing mechanism. T32/T43/T45 supply fault isolation, measurements and causal diagnosis. No prior database product experience is assumed.\n\n## Study sequence and teaching\n\n'
for i,row in enumerate(rows,1):text+=f'### T47.{i:02} — {row[0]}\n\n{row[5]}\n\nComplete [PR-T47-{i:02}](../projects/PR-T47-{i:02}.md). Keep three separate evidence items: derivation, executed implementation and repaired/transfer case.\n\n'
text+='## Reading guidance\n\nThe held OSPP second-edition persistent-storage volume supplies the inspected redo, repeatable replay and reclamation arguments. Public SQLite pages supply bounded alternative explanations of persistence assumptions and crash tests. Bayer/McCreight supplies the original B-tree balancing argument; the leaf-only values and separator convention here are an original B+tree contract. ARIES is listed as an unassigned foundational lead: only its IBM bibliographic record/abstract was inspected. No full ARIES implementation is implied. Assigned passages total 16 hours; use two additional hours to reconcile diagrams, assumptions and your own format.\n\n## Implementation projects\n\n| Milestone | Implementation | Verification | Total |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|\n'
for i,row in enumerate(rows,1):text+=f'| [PR-T47-{i:02}](../projects/PR-T47-{i:02}.md): {row[0]} | {row[2]} | {row[3]} | {row[1]} |\n'
text+='\nEvery project extends the same learner workspace. The public laboratory contains the API, compiling placeholder, adversarial harness, POSIX transport scaffold, format specification and staged hints. Complete solutions live only in the separate assessor distribution and require an explicit build selection. Named tests are mapped per project; passing them supplies bounded runtime evidence, not all objective credit.\n\n## Mastery gate and feedback\n\nSpend ten hours on cold review and an unseen fault schedule. Explain right-child equality, internal versus leaf split, minimum-key repair, free-page ownership, no-steal scratch, commit indeterminacy, checkpoint order and repeated recovery. Demonstrate the complete old/new semantic oracle and three killed wrong implementations. Minimize a failed schedule to the first invalid persistence transition. A setup failure or skipped POSIX case remains unavailable. Remediate the actual violated invariant, then repeat the trigger and one new variation.\n\n## Consolidation and transfer\n\nUse eight delayed hours to compare a new trace, optimize separator refresh without changing the API, and integrate a narrow VM host service or educational-kernel block backend. Existing implementation hours are charged once; new adapter evidence belongs to the integration milestone. Predict write amplification before counting it. Preserve old accepted evidence when making a format change; a new wire format needs a migration/rejection policy rather than silently reinterpreting old bytes.\n\n## Environment and limits\n\nOne exclusive caller serializes all accesses. Fixed capacities, seven-key nodes and full-image redo favor observable mechanisms over production throughput. Successful flush persists all preceding writes; tears affect only addressed pages; checksum collisions, lying flushes and later media corruption lie outside the atomicity argument. The harness samples five admitted persistence patterns at each selected write/flush boundary. It is not exhaustive over arbitrary subsets or tear positions and does not cut physical power. The preallocated-file route tests Linux API/reopen behavior; initial pathname durability and concurrent-process locking are separate. A complete runtime receipt records compiler/options/source hashes and actual results. Python contract checks do not replace those runs.\n'
write('curriculum/modules/T47.md',text)
